# Testing

Every new util, hook, service, store, component and screen gets a test in the same commit or the next one.

- Runner: Jest 30 + `@testing-library/react-native` 14. Run one file with `yarn jest <path>`; the full suite with `yarn test --ci`.
- Render through `renderWithProviders` (`@test-utils/renderWithProviders`). It wraps a fresh QueryClient (retry off), theme, i18n and a NavigationContainer, and takes `{ route?, authenticated?, theme?, language? }`.
- RNTL 14 is async: `await render(...)`, `await user.press(...)`, `await user.type(...)`. Make the test function `async`; do not wrap in `act()`.
- Query with `screen`. **Prefer `getByRole`** (with `name`), then `getByLabelText` / `getByText`. `getByTestId` only when nothing accessible exists (a lint warning, `testing-library/prefer-screen-queries` is an error).
- Network goes through **MSW** (`src/test-utils/msw/server.ts`, handlers in `msw/handlers/<domain>.ts`). Never mock `axios` or `fetch` by hand. Use factories from `@test-utils/factories/*` for data.
- Test files sit next to the source: `Button.test.tsx`, `useDebounce.test.ts`, `auth.store.test.ts`. Only test files, stories and `src/test-utils/**` may import `@test-utils/*`.
- **Spec-linked tests:** the test name starts with the AC ID from the spec: `it('AC-1: navigates to Home after valid login', ...)`. Maestro flows list AC IDs in `tags:`. `yarn spec:check` fails when an AC in an `implemented` or `verified` spec has no linked test.
- Cover render, interaction, error/empty/loading states and a11y role/state for components. Test behavior, not implementation details or snapshots of whole trees.
- Mock only native modules; they are already mocked in `jest.setup.ts` (MMKV, Keychain, NetInfo, Reanimated, Unistyles, ...).
- `scripts/**` tests use `node --test` (`yarn test:ai-log`, `yarn test:ai-sync`), not Jest.

```tsx
// ✅
it('AC-2: shows an error for a wrong password', async () => {
  const { user } = await renderWithProviders(<LoginScreen />);
  await user.type(screen.getByLabelText('Password'), 'wrong');
  await user.press(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign in' }));
  expect(await screen.findByRole('alert')).toBeOnTheScreen();
});

// ❌ test id query, no AC link, hand-mocked network, enzyme-style internals
it('works', () => {
  jest.spyOn(axios, 'post').mockResolvedValue({});
  render(<LoginScreen />);
  fireEvent.press(screen.getByTestId('login.submit-button'));
});
```
